      {
        "id": 142650,
        "name": "morph147",
        "username": "morph147",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/839c29/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-15T03:39:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So after e3 day 1 this is my thoughts</p><p>mario maker: looks insane to play. Worry is on length of time to make a level and the status on Wii U and how there isn't much reason to buy it in my opinion.</p><p>bethdesa showcase: doom looks good but not my cup of tea. Dishonored I am excited for but need to play the first one before I know for sure if I care about it. Fallout 4 looks like a lot of fun and it's great that it will be out In November. Love elder scrolls so this may be up my alley but not sure how much I care about the first person shooter aspect, never been a big fan but may give it a try once the price drops or just get fallout 3. Elder scrolls was my biggest disappointment. Was hoping for news on 6 but with online just coming out it appears they wanted to focus on that. Also disappointed we didn't get more details on the first expansion since game has been out for a year at this point on pc but for the time being the few clips I did see cant wait. Going to check out the fallout iPad game when it comes out later tonight called fallout shelter since it's completely free.&nbsp;</p><p>Ultimately so far everything I have seen looks good. Nothing yet that will ultimately end up on my Christmas list as must haves but a couple that I would dig out of the bargain bin later down the road or rent to try it out. So I will give the day a B overall. Lots to see tomorrow, mainly the important shows like Sony, ubisoft and electronic arts. May check out the less important ones like Microsoft just because sometimes they show off stuff that will be on the better system aka ps4 later down the road</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
